# CeraLive — DEVELOPMENT / DEBUG package DELTA (variant-gated, NOT a family delta)
#
# This is the file `removed.md` §(e) forward-referenced as "a future
# packages/development.delta.list may formalize this". It is now real.
#
# ============================================================================
# THIS LIST IS INSTALLED **ONLY** WHEN `CERALIVE_DEBUG_IMAGE=1`.
# ============================================================================
#
# A production build (`CERALIVE_DEBUG_IMAGE` unset or `0`) resolves
# `shared.list` + the resolved `<family>.delta.list` and NOTHING from this file —
# the production package set is byte-identical to what it was before this file
# existed. `lib/orchestrate.sh` appends this list to `$SHARED_PACKAGES` only on
# the debug branch of the seam, and every `*.delta.list` directory glob in the
# repo (`lib/parity-check.sh`, `tests/package-migration-coverage.sh`,
# `tests/realhw-suite.sh`) skips this file by name unless that same flag is set.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS IS NOT A `<family>.delta.list`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `rk3588.delta.list` / `x86_64.delta.list` are keyed on the resolved board
# FAMILY and are selected by `orchestrate.sh` as `${FAMILY}.delta.list`. This
# file is keyed on the BUILD VARIANT instead, so it is arch/family-independent
# and is never reachable through the family lookup — `FAMILY=development` is not
# a family, no such manifest exists, and `resolve.py` would reject it. The
# filename keeps the `.delta.list` suffix because it IS a delta over
# `shared.list` in exactly the same format; the consumers discriminate by name.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RELATIONSHIP TO THE `debug-toolset` SYSEXT ADD-ON — BOTH, NOT EITHER
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `v2/manifests/addons/debug-toolset.json` stays EXACTLY as it is and remains
# the FIELD-DIAGNOSTICS path: an operator installs it at runtime, on a
# production image, over the network, with no reflash. Nothing in this file
# changes that add-on, its descriptor, its build (`lib/build-feature-sysext.sh`
# reads a `--deb-staging` tree and never reads any `*.list`), or its R2
# delivery path.
#
# This list is the BENCH path instead: packages baked into an explicitly-marked
# debug image at build time, so a developer debugging the boot/first-boot window
# has them before any network or add-on manager exists. The T17 fifteen below
# are deliberately the SAME set the add-on carries, so the two paths give the
# same toolbox and an operator never has to learn which one they are on.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NO DUPLICATION (the same rule `removed.md` states for the family deltas)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every package below was verified ABSENT from `shared.list` — a duplicate would
# make the "debug == production + exactly this delta" identity untrue and is
# pinned by `tests/manifest.bats` §30.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MEASURED EFFECT (rock-5b-plus, real wet builds, 2026-08-08)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   production  1,416,232,960 B   553 packages
#   debug       1,477,160,960 B   595 packages   (+60,928,000 B = +58.11 MiB)
#
# 42 packages added (these 18 + 24 transitive deps), ZERO removed. Debug headroom
# under the 1.5 GB absolute ceiling is 22,839,040 B (21.78 MiB) — so this list is
# NOT free to grow without measuring. The relative size-baseline comparison is
# deliberately SKIPPED for a debug build (the committed baseline is a production
# artifact); the absolute ceiling still applies to both variants.
#
# Exactly TWO systemd units differ between the two rootfs trees:
#   ssh.service      — INTENDED, the debug seam's documented access behaviour.
#   vnstat.service   — a side effect of Debian's preset for the `vnstat` package.
#                      Kept: vnstat's whole function is cumulative accounting, and
#                      it collects nothing unless its daemon runs. Debug-only.
# `pulseaudio` adds NO system unit (verified in the built rootfs) — see its note.
#
# Format: one package per line; `#` comments justify entries.

# --- Interpreter (the plan's headline addition) -------------------------------
python3                  # NOT in the production image at all (verified against a
                         # real production rootfs: 552 installed packages, zero
                         # python3*). Nothing in the shipped runtime is written in
                         # Python — the build-side tooling that is (resolve.py,
                         # validate-manifests.py) runs on the BUILD HOST, never on
                         # the device. So this is a genuine debug-only addition and
                         # is the cleanest content-diff probe for the two variants.

# --- Kernel/syscall + wire tracing (ceraui-base DEVELOPMENT, removed.md §(e)) --
strace                   # syscall tracing — the first tool reached for when a
                         # capture/encode process blocks or dies with no log.
tcpdump                  # packet capture for the bonded-uplink path; the SRTLA
                         # link math is invisible without it on a live board.

# --- The T17 debug-toolset seed set (removed.md §(h)) -------------------------
# These fifteen were moved OUT of the mandatory `shared.list` by the T17 slimming
# pass, each verified to have no runtime consumer in CeraUI, cerastream, srtla or
# the mkosi runtime postinst. They are the add-on's payload and are re-listed here
# so the baked debug image carries the identical toolbox.
alsa-utils               # alsamixer/aplay/arecord — ALSA-level audio diagnosis.
pulseaudio               # ships /usr/bin/pulseaudio, in the add-on's `provides`.
                         # INERT unless invoked: bookworm ships only USER units
                         # (/usr/lib/systemd/user/pulseaudio.{service,socket}) and
                         # this appliance has no user session, so it never
                         # autostarts and never contends with `alsasrc` for the
                         # capture device. Do NOT enable it system-wide.
usbutils                 # lsusb — USB enumeration during a detach/replug drill.
pciutils                 # lspci — PCI introspection (NIC/WiFi/NVMe bring-up).
lsof                     # which process holds the capture fd.
i2c-tools                # i2cdetect — sensor/EEPROM board bring-up.
can-utils                # candump — CAN tooling; no CeraLive datapath uses CAN.
htop                     # interactive process monitor.
iotop                    # IO monitor for storage-bound encode/record work.
nethogs                  # per-process bandwidth, for link-saturation debugging.
vnstat                   # cumulative traffic accounting.
nano                     # on-box editor.
iperf3                   # bonded-link throughput testing.
socat                    # socket relay. NOTE: the first-boot captive portal
                         # (`runtime/ceralive-portal.sh`) is deliberately pure
                         # bash BECAUSE socat is not in the production image —
                         # its presence here must NOT be read as permission to
                         # reintroduce a socat dependency into any runtime path.
netcat-openbsd           # nc connectivity probing (same caveat as socat).
